{"name":"Aura","hex":"#b2a8a1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Aura","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A diminutive of the female given name Aurelia, from Latin.","A minor female deity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Aura"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aura (paranormal)","blocks":[{"text":"In parapsychology and some spiritual traditions, an aura, or energy field, is said to be an emanation produced by and surrounding the body of a person, animal or object, unique to the individual, and which is typically regarded to be an ever present and essential part of its being. In some esoteric positions, the aura is described as a subtle body. Psychics and holistic medicine practitioners often claim to have the ability to see the size, color and type of vibration of an aura."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Aura_diagram.png/330px-Aura_diagram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aura_(paranormal)","wikidata":"Q1154226"},{"title":"Aura (symptom)","blocks":[{"text":"An aura is a perceptual disturbance experienced by some with epilepsy or migraine. An epileptic aura is a form of minor seizure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Migraine_aura.jpg/330px-Migraine_aura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aura_(symptom)","wikidata":"Q739481"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg/250px-Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Lea